# M0.3 — MACE full-cell base run (`pair_style mace`, no overlay, no hybrid).
#        This is the baseline every other MACE item is compared against, and
#        the reference energy for M0.4's constant-offset check.
#
# Geometry: bilayer_mos2.data from make_geometries.py — 24 atoms, 4 atom types.
# TYPE LAYOUT:
#   1 = Mo layer 1   2 = S layer 1
#   3 = Mo layer 2   4 = S layer 2
# Every type maps to a real element: `pair_style mace` rejects NULL type maps
# (ACEsuit #1314), so MACE is scoped to full-cell coverage.
#
# Run (Kokkos, one GPU, one MPI rank — the pair style is used with
# no_domain_decomposition):
#       $PREFIX/lammps-mace/build/lmp -k on g 1 -sf kk -in m0_3_mace_fullcell.in
#
# PASS: 20 steps complete; finite total energy and forces; record E_pair at
#       step 0 — M0.4 compares against it.

units metal
atom_style atomic
read_data bilayer_mos2.data
pair_style mace no_domain_decomposition
pair_coeff * * mace mace.model-lammps.pt Mo S Mo S
# Masses are also in the data file; repeated here so the deck is self-contained.
mass 1 95.95   # Mo
mass 2 32.06   # S
mass 3 95.95   # Mo
mass 4 32.06   # S
thermo 1
run 0
fix nve all nve
run 20
